# xin — the modern replacement for the old linux-rhel bundle. Distro-agnostic:
# these same modules install on Fedora/RHEL (dnf), Debian/Ubuntu (apt), Arch,
# Alpine and Void. rust is listed first as a toolchain prerequisite (manifest
# order is the dependency graph, §4). foot ships its own rice-owned palette below.
#
# alacritty is the terminal here rather than ghostty: this rice runs on hosts
# whose GPU cannot give a GPU terminal an OpenGL context (Ghostty wants 4.3,
# kitty 3.3, an Ironlake-era iGPU tops out at 2.1), and Alacritty's GLES2
# fallback renderer starts there. It ships this rice's palette in
# config/alacritty/. yazi is listed after it because the two are paired: with no
# image protocol in Alacritty, yazi previews images through the chafa that
# modules/yazi.sh installs.
rust
starship
zsh
fastfetch
btop
htop
ncdu
alacritty
yazi